          "text": "{\"regions\":{\"r2\":{\"type\":\"stanza_note\",\"lines\":[{\"n\":1,\"text\":\"\u092a\u0930\u0902 \u092f\u0938\u094d\u092f\u093e\u0903 \u0964 with an eye solely to wealth; greedy. \u0935\u0926\u093e\u0928\u094d\u092f-liberal;\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":2,\"text\":\"munificent. \u0928\u093f\u0924\u094d\u092f may be taken either as adj. or adv. in the\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":3,\"text\":\"dissolution of the compounds, \u0928\u093f\u0924\u094d\u092f\u0935\u094d\u092f\u092f and \u092a\u094d\u0930\u091a\u0941\u0930\u0928\u093f\u0924\u094d\u092f\u0927\u0928\u093e\u0917\u092e\u093e. The\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":4,\"text\":\"fig. is \u0909\u092a\u092e\u093e.\",\"end\":\"space\"}],\"uncertain\":true,\"note\":\"The Sanskrit compound in line 3 is difficult to read.\"},\"r3\":{\"type\":\"stanza_note\",\"lines\":[{\"n\":1,\"text\":\"Sl. 48. \u0906\u091c\u094d\u091e\u093e\u2014power to enforce command. R\u00e2mrshi con-\",\"end\":\"hyphen\"},{\"n\":2,\"text\":\"siders the word \u092c\u094d\u0930\u093e\u0939\u094d\u092e\u0923\u093e\u0928\u093e\u092e\u094d to be an \u0909\u092a\u0932\u0915\u094d\u0937\u0923 i. e. as in-\",\"end\":\"hyphen\"},{\"n\":3,\"text\":\"cluding all people. The Br\u00e2hma\u1e47as are specially mentioned as\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":4,\"text\":\"most deserving help and protection, their priestly avocation\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":5,\"text\":\"making it impossible for them to defend themselves with arms\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":6,\"text\":\"&c. \u092f\u0947\u0937\u093e\u0902 \u090f\u0924\u0947 &c. who have not gained these six qualities (special\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":7,\"text\":\"advantages ). \u092a\u093e\u0930\u094d\u0925\u093f\u0935\u094b\u092a\u093e\u0936\u094d\u0930\u092f\u2014taking shelter with a king i. e.\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":8,\"text\":\"becoming royal servants or favourites. Or \u092a\u093e\u0930\u094d\u0925\u093f\u0935 may be taken\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":9,\"text\":\"as Voc. singular; in this case \u0924\u0947\u0937\u093e\u0902 may refere to kings; what is\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":10,\"text\":\"the use of resorting to those kings who do not &c.\",\"end\":\"space\"}],\"uncertain\":false,\"note\":null},\"r4\":{\"type\":\"stanza_note\",\"lines\":[{\"n\":1,\"text\":\"Sl. 49. \u092e\u0930\u0941\u0938\u094d\u0925\u0932\u0947\u2014\u092e\u0930\u0941 is the waterless tract now known as\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":2,\"text\":\"M\u00e2r w\u00e2r. \u092e\u094d\u0930\u093f\u092f\u0928\u094d\u0924\u0947\u093d\u0938\u094d\u092e\u093f\u0928\u094d \u092d\u0942\u0924\u093e\u0928\u093f \u091c\u0932\u093e\u092d\u093e\u0935\u093e\u0924\u094d \u0907\u0924\u093f \u092e\u0930\u0941\u0903, fr. \u092e\u0943+\u0909 Un. I. 7.\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":3,\"text\":\"\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":4,\"text\":\"\u092e\u0947\u0930\u094c\u2014on the mountain Meru, the store-house of wealth. Accord-\",\"end\":\"hyphen\"},{\"n\":5,\"text\":\"ing to the Pur\u00e2\u1e47as the mountain Meru is formed of gold and\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":6,\"text\":\"jewels. It is the loftiest mountain on earth and the centre\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":7,\"text\":\"round which the whole firmament revolves. \u0915\u0943\u092a\u0923\u093e\u0902 \u0935\u0943\u0924\u094d\u0924\u093f\u0902 \u092e\u093e \u0915\u0943\u0925\u093e\u0903\u2014\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":8,\"text\":\"do not act or behave in an abject manner. The last line shows\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":9,\"text\":\"that on the capacity of a man depends his fortune, and it should\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":10,\"text\":\"be rightly understood to counteract the effect of the first which\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":11,\"text\":\"is fatalistic. The fig. is \u0926\u0943\u0937\u094d\u091f\u093e\u0928\u094d\u0924. See sl. 57.\",\"end\":\"space\"}],\"uncertain\":true,\"note\":\"The Sanskrit derivation in line 2 and its suffix are difficult to read.\"},\"r5\":{\"type\":\"stanza_note\",\"lines\":[{\"n\":1,\"text\":\"\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":2,\"text\":\"Sl. 50. \u0917\u094b\u091a\u0930\u2014moving within the range of the senses ( \u0917\u094b );\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":3,\"text\":\"hence, known. See supra sl. 16. \u0915\u093e\u0930\u094d\u092a\u0923\u094d\u092f\u094b\u0915\u094d\u0924\u093f\u0903\u2014words expressive\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":4,\"text\":\"of our pitiful condition, supplication. The fig. here is \u0905\u092a\u094d\u0930\u0938\u094d\u0924\u0941\u0924\u092a\u094d\u0930\u0936\u0902-\",\"end\":\"hyphen\"},{\"n\":5,\"text\":\"\u0938\u093e. Some liberal person is addressed with these words which\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":6,\"text\":\"apparently refer to the cloud. \u0905\u092a\u094d\u0930\u0938\u094d\u0924\u0941\u0924\u092a\u094d\u0930\u0936\u0902\u0938\u093e is thus defined:\u2014\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":7,\"text\":\"\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":8,\"text\":\"\u0905\u092a\u094d\u0930\u0938\u094d\u0924\u0941\u0924\u092a\u094d\u0930\u0936\u0902\u0938\u093e \u0938\u093e \u092f\u093e \u0938\u0948\u0935 \u092a\u094d\u0930\u0938\u094d\u0924\u0941\u0924\u093e\u0936\u094d\u0930\u092f\u093e K. P. X.\",\"end\":\"space\"}],\"uncertain\":false,\"note\":null},\"r6\":{\"type\":\"stanza_note\",\"lines\":[{\"n\":1,\"text\":\"Sl. 51. \u0938\u093e\u0935\u0927\u093e\u0928\u092e\u0928\u0938\u093e\u2014with close or assiduous attention.\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":2,\"text\":\"\u090f\u0924\u093e\u0926\u0943\u0936\u093e\u0903\u2014such, referring to \u091a\u093e\u0924\u0915\u093e\u0927\u093e\u0930 in the above S'loka. Al-\",\"end\":\"hyphen\"},{\"n\":3,\"text\":\"though the slokas are not much connected with each other still\",\"end\":\"space\"}],\"uncertain\":true,\"note\":\"The Sanskrit word referring to the previous stanza is not entirely clear.\"},\"r1\":{\"type\":\"page_number\",\"lines\":[{\"n\":1,\"text\":\"( 23 )\",\"end\":\"space\"}],\"uncertain\":false,\"note\":null}},\"units\":[{\"id\":\"u1\",\"type\":\"notes\",\"number\":null,\"label\":null,\"open_start\":true,\"open_end\":true,\"children\":[\"u2\",\"u3\",\"u4\",\"u5\",\"u6\"]},{\"id\":\"u2\",\"type\":\"stanza_note\",\"number\":\"47\",\"label\":null,\"open_start\":true,\"open_end\":false,\"children\":[\"r2\"]},{\"id\":\"u3\",\"type\":\"stanza_note\",\"number\":\"48\",\"label\":null,\"open_start\":false,\"open_end\":false,\"children\":[\"r3\"]},{\"id\":\"u4\",\"type\":\"stanza_note\",\"number\":\"49\",\"label\":null,\"open_start\":false,\"open_end\":false,\"children\":[\"r4\"]},{\"id\":\"u5\",\"type\":\"stanza_note\",\"number\":\"50\",\"label\":null,\"open_start\":false,\"open_end\":false,\"children\":[\"r5\"]},{\"id\":\"u6\",\"type\":\"stanza_note\",\"number\":\"51\",\"label\":null,\"open_start\":false,\"open_end\":true,\"children\":[\"r6\"]}],\"flows\":[{\"flow\":\"main\",\"units\":[\"u1\"]}],\"relations\":[]}"
        }
